## Schema & migrations

The generated TypeORM DataSource in `src/generated/generated.module.ts` runs with
**`synchronize: true`**. On every boot TypeORM inspects the `@Entity` classes and creates or
updates the SQLite tables to match — so there is **no migration step in development** and no
migration files are generated.

`synchronize: true` is convenient but unsafe for production (it can drop or alter columns to
follow the entities). Before deploying:

1. Set `synchronize: false` in `generated.module.ts`.
2. Add a TypeORM CLI DataSource and generate/run migrations, e.g.
   `npx typeorm migration:generate ./migrations/Init -d ./data-source.ts` then
   `npx typeorm migration:run -d ./data-source.ts`.

